export abstract anchor FactoryDescriptor:
    commandInvocation:
        Subcommand names in the standard surface are fixed. Each project has a
        descriptor at `.factory/project.json`, generated during onboarding or
        scaffolding, that records how the factory is invoked. Packaged skills
        and engineers read the descriptor before operating the factory. The
        outer executable name, packaging, and technology remain project choices.
        The invocation array has at least one element. argv[0] is invocation[0];
        invocation[1..] are fixed arguments. The standard subcommand is appended
        immediately after the invocation array, and the subcommand's own
        arguments follow it. No global option is inserted between them. cwd
        applies to the invocation and every subcommand.
    descriptorSchema:
        The descriptor is UTF-8 JSON with a schemaVersion. The current version
        is 1 and the supported maximum is 1. Required fields are schemaVersion,
        invocation as an array of one or more non-empty strings, config as a
        project-relative path, specVersion as an immutable full commit SHA or
        exact tag, and builtAgainstSpecVersion as the immutable implementation
        baseline. An empty invocation fails validation.
        Optional fields are cwd, an environment map of string values, dashboard
        as an http or https URL, capabilities as an array of focus or optimize,
        implementationVersion, name, and configDigest as a SHA-256 digest of
        the loaded configuration. An empty capabilities array means none are
        declared.
        Unknown fields are preserved on rewrite and ignored by readers. An
        unsupported newer schemaVersion is a clear error. A missing or invalid
        required field is an error. Writes are atomic and serialized by the
        project lock.
    descriptorPaths:
        The project root is the parent of `.factory`. Descriptor discovery
        searches upward from the working directory and refuses when multiple
        descriptors are found. Config and relative invocation paths resolve from
        the root. Absolute paths, parent traversal, and symlinks escaping the
        root after canonicalization are rejected. cwd is containment-checked.
        invocation[0] and relative fixed arguments resolve from the root before
        cwd applies. cwd defaults to the project root and never changes argument
        resolution or descriptor discovery. argv[0] resolves through PATH unless
        it contains a path separator, in which case it resolves from the root.
        PATH comes from the process environment and cannot be overridden by the
        descriptor or wiring. Descriptor environment overlays the process
        environment for non-PATH keys; later entries override earlier ones.
    descriptorMigration:
        Schema changes increment schemaVersion. Older unsupported versions are
        refused with an explicit upgrade path that is versioned, backed up,
        idempotent, and preserves unknown fields. Newer versions are refused.
        Validation checks types, containment, invocation executability without
        executing it, config existence, capability names for the schema version,
        and that specVersion resolves against the tether lock. Secrets are
        rejected in the environment map by key pattern as a best effort.
